    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "You are building a neural network to predict whether a user will like a particular video on an online video app.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Create a machine learning pipeline with a single-layer neural network. The pipeline should have a `StandardScaler` and an `SGDRegressor`.\r\n2. Fit the model to the training inputs and outputs. Run the program and take note of the mean squared error value for your network.\r\n3. Replace the `SGDRegressor` model with an `MLPRegressor`, so that the network can use hidden layers. Run the program and take note of the mean squared error value. Is it better?\r\n4. Try experimenting with the number of units in the hidden layer and the number of iterations. What values lead to a low mean squared error? (Hint: try at least 5 hidden layer units and at least 2000 iterations.)\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nTo create a pipeline, use the `make_pipeline` function. For the arguments, use a scaler like `StandardScaler()` and a model like `SGDRegressor()`. \r\n\r\nTo create a multi-layer neural network that has a hidden layer with `M` units and that trains for up to `N` iterations, use code like\r\n\r\n```python\r\nMLPRegressor(hidden_layer_sizes=(M,), max_iter=N)\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhere `M` and `N` are numbers that you choose.\r\n",
